#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119543 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "fd3cb5b1-f16e-5a52-82e4-25bbbd1c4fe7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4789" :question/problem "Find $s,$ if $3\\mathbf{a_1}+s\\mathbf{a_2} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/assets/df62636427555a986454d8d2787e110eb664771f5a74a38fdaa99ec593643729.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $s$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+s{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $s=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119544 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "548ef945-392b-5e75-9b60-14f4e2de6261" :question/math-academy-id "e-4790" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{x},$ if $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/assets/93311059b2929dfac5a7dc2019e4591534fdcf3c416486ffdfc78ece16901ca4.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $\\mathbf{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119545 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "13ebde04-8518-5837-9420-c9487debc562" :question/math-academy-id "e-4791" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/assets/cc8a77d53637f5523dcdadd79ea3a282efe30b96aaeb9ec31fce1f39d4006186.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then what is $x_1+x_2?$" :question/worked-solution "If $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -{x}_{1}=-5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain $x_1=5,$ which we substitute into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ 4(5)+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 3(5)+(-15) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15,$ which means\n\n$$\n5 \\mathbf{c_1}-15 \\mathbf{c_2} = \\mathbf{d}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2=5-15=-10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119593 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "d9beff9d-db58-540f-811e-a07fb77d3d92" :question/math-academy-id "e-6191" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/assets/9f5f9de266fac1e593ea58a3406ff88ccecb3a64963d55367297404360771d83.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{a}_2 + x_3\\mathbf{a}_3 = \\mathbf b,$ then what is $x_1+x_2+x_3?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{b}$ is a linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{a_1}, \\,\\mathbf{a_2}$ and $\\mathbf{a_3}$ with coefficients $x_1,\\, x_2$ and $x_3,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/assets/4d3cb5eb82dd012582c78fc2c1201c62f99779d92974aba2a61f5a6bce8b91b9.png)\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 = 2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_3=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+2(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=-3, x_2=-1, x_3=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3 \\mathbf{a_1}- \\mathbf{a_2} +2 \\mathbf{a_3}= \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2+x_3=-3-1+2=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "896ea9d6-d71a-55be-b137-a5e8ac75f68b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321255} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1b900c-9290-573e-8125-c6bec2f64905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321256} {:answer/id #uuid "1176f2ad-3206-5c46-9a89-46355b922602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321257} {:answer/id #uuid "4e4f0f10-e223-5ad9-92de-237ec6ada06a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321258} {:answer/id #uuid "0ccb8b67-8dc0-5b12-86be-ddd6cb929af2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c1b900c-9290-573e-8125-c6bec2f64905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321256} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a6f583-b3f7-5ed3-b22e-5a4039b73977" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a8f533b-003a-5522-aad6-99090100d40d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105152" :question/problem "Find $h$, if $3{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $h$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+h[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ h[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ h[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $h=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60be7523-d278-5123-b879-2344e0c92d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387252} {:answer/id #uuid "fabf58c5-c945-5500-a51f-3b7189d80b10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387253} {:answer/id #uuid "804425ea-56ef-547a-97e1-89f3b3f4b848" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387254} {:answer/id #uuid "0a4a21f9-1bac-5bff-8a85-463cfabd027c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387255} {:answer/id #uuid "52779063-8881-5e5b-b003-3ea9eafa4201" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fabf58c5-c945-5500-a51f-3b7189d80b10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387253} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f3f3ee2-b7cd-5dec-a437-c3d6f8a9ddfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e3d35d4-4023-5683-a525-12eaa9fbede7" :question/math-academy-id "q-105161" :question/problem "Find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$ given that $7a+4x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7a+4x & =b \\\\ 4x & =b-7a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}(b-7a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]-7[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-2-1=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "977281d2-30c8-5ffb-a3ec-10faa5aa31e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387259} {:answer/id #uuid "1cdf8288-04f8-58a2-90cd-e3b5d024ba20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387260} {:answer/id #uuid "1fc364fe-15f1-5fc9-b62b-128302726ace" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387261} {:answer/id #uuid "d74b43a7-9d8f-5d05-b2d0-00d7709dde21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387262} {:answer/id #uuid "4250256c-1125-542a-819f-1aa213362e31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d74b43a7-9d8f-5d05-b2d0-00d7709dde21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387262} :answer-field/id #uuid "6990e5c8-3c63-576d-8ca2-ec8c1c5d88b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9541c7b4-0663-5396-9a08-887584cc6208" :question/math-academy-id "q-105168" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ -8{x}_{2} \\\\ 6{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=-5 \\\\ {x}_{3}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=6.$ Substituting ${x}_{3}=6$ into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-6=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{3}=6$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(1)+2(6)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-7.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-7$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=6,$ which means \n\n$$\n-7{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}+6{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-7+1+6=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387264 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1594f466-029c-538a-927c-f05ba108777d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387266} {:answer/id #uuid "77a070d1-a7e0-5a87-b628-841a1a7dc211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387267} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf7cfc0-7f0a-5781-b257-35a5fcc09ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387268} {:answer/id #uuid "b8dbc27d-8fad-5d1d-a690-989d77281404" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387269} {:answer/id #uuid "43094605-3da8-5055-b24e-0fac50416cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdf7cfc0-7f0a-5781-b257-35a5fcc09ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387268} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca0ebbbb-330e-54e1-b8d2-6e8546cd0563" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fe99bc13-e7dd-5467-8c41-093bc5c5d798" :question/math-academy-id "q-105169" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 5{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 6{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ -8{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=-13 \\\\ 0=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=8$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eff636f3-b198-59d4-9f2f-810a6c64ce12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387273} {:answer/id #uuid "e51413da-6e3e-58b6-9bfc-725f3bc25cc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387274} {:answer/id #uuid "44b35dcf-92af-52dc-9983-49175277bdb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387275} {:answer/id #uuid "aad0eb49-3784-58fd-ab15-3d2fb2f7ee9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387276} {:answer/id #uuid "965ca52f-2190-5554-871c-69ac7d7ab359" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e51413da-6e3e-58b6-9bfc-725f3bc25cc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387274} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c01106d-fd1a-5c80-a154-36c814c4fdca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6ab3f90e-8765-500f-9621-dff08b568cfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-105170" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2} \\\\ 8{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{3} \\\\ -7{x}_{3} \\\\ 14{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 7 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 14 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 7 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 14 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 14 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 0=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=-3$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "700a2a9b-8d44-5bdb-992b-933cda3741d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387280} {:answer/id #uuid "276a1753-bd27-5193-9808-68e8fb1835bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387281} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e414d5-ba6a-510d-b844-a5c7d5b0b3a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387282} {:answer/id #uuid "056e2068-0aa6-5e4a-8bcd-393b685c6c6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387283} {:answer/id #uuid "a08d6e7b-ba52-5254-9264-cc7d903823d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "056e2068-0aa6-5e4a-8bcd-393b685c6c6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387283} :answer-field/id #uuid "f721ebcd-0067-5fd7-8a67-cc4bc4eef629" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e4ac70ed-e31e-5734-ad94-c0291cd01d10" :question/math-academy-id "q-34051" :question/problem "Find $k$, if $2{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+k[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $k=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa7db68f-227f-5c5e-af41-77ea4c96ae74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387287} {:answer/id #uuid "5b861c8b-daf5-5538-9a76-de42fe6f0e5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387288} {:answer/id #uuid "55b366fc-fc51-5adb-94bd-ecb8daf0b3b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387289} {:answer/id #uuid "bad6f831-5493-5bba-bc46-12dc352c1dac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387290} {:answer/id #uuid "72b6166d-b970-5044-b11e-dc42ad1ab98e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bad6f831-5493-5bba-bc46-12dc352c1dac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387290} :answer-field/id #uuid "e65392a6-2d7a-5d95-9752-2ee839aa3f11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd09a13d-8779-54f4-a062-8c9f261baebd" :question/math-academy-id "q-34052" :question/problem "Find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$ given that $3a-5x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -22 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-5x & =b \\\\ -5x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}([\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -22 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3-1=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08db849c-1e93-5027-ba6a-5fbd72b9f2f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387294} {:answer/id #uuid "5e49b773-534b-581c-8c6f-57a62f5a747a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387295} {:answer/id #uuid "2e11d248-33ab-5ec2-8f2f-1a93696f2ec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387296} {:answer/id #uuid "826d0304-cb45-5dd1-b229-25c007c1810b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387297} {:answer/id #uuid "57d258b0-c05c-5bfb-ab7d-d13e76b36a4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08db849c-1e93-5027-ba6a-5fbd72b9f2f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387294} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8503df4-2d3d-55aa-a4be-e7b5009dfe11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a6749d3-0128-5cc2-8904-1ac573ac629e" :question/math-academy-id "q-34241" :question/problem "Find $j$, if ${a}_{1}-j{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $j$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}-j{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-j[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ j[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ j[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $j=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "382d93ad-2e02-5155-92da-be5439a4d870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321297} {:answer/id #uuid "7a5fc2fa-5f72-5ad0-8fd1-69aef1192d54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321298} {:answer/id #uuid "1f5d0608-98d6-5575-8b82-82ab03f3b03c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321299} {:answer/id #uuid "f20cb265-08c1-578b-9e9d-7fea1f9cb223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321300} {:answer/id #uuid "bf9c0a5e-f0ac-5af4-9e4c-4aca14345995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "382d93ad-2e02-5155-92da-be5439a4d870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321297} :answer-field/id #uuid "e62db11a-3245-5286-acf2-e78cc28d847e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49d86e24-f480-5ade-b4df-5af4f350fca2" :question/math-academy-id "q-34242" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0=4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first equation is a false statement. Hence,the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a729f364-6e1f-5f3c-8aac-bad6ac301733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118174} {:answer/id #uuid "d4202c24-f6d4-545b-8aba-4b4b3d5ccbfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118175} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0821b9-32ad-5173-99fe-5be909f0e46c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118176} {:answer/id #uuid "52425281-c631-56c6-9881-021bd2376c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118177} {:answer/id #uuid "6a747503-e283-5be3-a6e7-56347bfe62d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4202c24-f6d4-545b-8aba-4b4b3d5ccbfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118175} :answer-field/id #uuid "02e1fd9c-0606-50c7-aadd-cc07a38a34d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "14248ec5-b54c-565b-8b43-275a9e097f62" :question/math-academy-id "q-34568" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $3$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13{x}_{2} & =13\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4(1) & =3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=1$ into the third equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ 5(1)+2(1) & =5 \\\\ 7 & =5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f77e537-174a-5743-a569-48878d1be8f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387301} {:answer/id #uuid "d041a5c1-9af3-5c9d-b744-73203348e960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387302} {:answer/id #uuid "92f3364d-c08b-5a7a-