er/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387315} {:answer/id #uuid "b41db642-8cd7-5a66-af77-1ec2a6149bcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387316} {:answer/id #uuid "ce92e4cf-0b15-5228-901f-116d14806fd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387317} {:answer/id #uuid "026e7904-3b5e-52e0-bf06-5df1e87eaff1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387318} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea7853e-b3c5-5a81-b9d7-84fd98dadd1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b41db642-8cd7-5a66-af77-1ec2a6149bcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387316} :answer-field/id #uuid "da2c4319-288d-5947-bab0-1574b5ea2210" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2567000b-57ae-5d7c-b37b-917f1f640392" :question/math-academy-id "q-73937" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $2a+5x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -30 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+5x & =b \\\\ 5x & =b-2a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{5}(b-2a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{5}([\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -30 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 40\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29475f1b-ddc2-5713-a560-ff80acf114a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321332} {:answer/id #uuid "feec4427-c165-5d44-850a-f46341050c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321333} {:answer/id #uuid "279fa3c9-cd8e-53ce-bcf5-08f02de7d37b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321334} {:answer/id #uuid "82e88e8d-cabf-599f-abaa-d031639540b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321335} {:answer/id #uuid "125e02f4-7360-5425-9504-fbee83158e4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feec4427-c165-5d44-850a-f46341050c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321333} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c395a36-ec62-59c1-ab1e-9dee4bd9949b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4aa4d92-2f8e-50b3-bd53-f6e46489ca0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73951" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$\n." :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-11 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the second and the third  equations we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1} & =-16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ into the third equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-2)+{x}_{2}=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =3 \\\\ (-2)+2(3) & =3 \\\\ 4 & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9e1e9a2-153d-517b-ab67-7837c2168555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321339} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1b1e93-7840-5a85-a773-ae87f2b5dd73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321340} {:answer/id #uuid "49de6bee-41ab-548b-bd49-2d7003a678e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321341} {:answer/id #uuid "c9dc09a7-17e3-52a0-b09e-3b562d4778e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321342} {:answer/id #uuid "e027474a-a491-5523-a95b-98e263653e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49de6bee-41ab-548b-bd49-2d7003a678e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321341} :answer-field/id #uuid "b90369b5-0596-5750-b1d1-222b297e0373" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49280f22-8d86-589c-8580-452aa67d8a42" :question/math-academy-id "q-73952" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-7 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equation we get\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{2}=-8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{2}=4$ into the first equation yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & =-7 \\\\ {x}_{1}-(4) & =-7 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-7+4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =6 \\\\ 2(-3)+3(4) & =6 \\\\ 6 & =6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3+4=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1a8f928-83ab-5fb2-af01-ba09b4e8d2b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387322} {:answer/id #uuid "0d63f362-3186-5550-a8f1-93658696f7e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387323} {:answer/id #uuid "05abe5d3-534a-59e4-849a-fecf054ff7dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387324} {:answer/id #uuid "a21f3728-530f-5844-a211-ed2eb4dfaf55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387325} {:answer/id #uuid "3f6677ce-6f4b-5849-85bc-d4532e2b5edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f6677ce-6f4b-5849-85bc-d4532e2b5edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387326} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d9dc079-ace9-597d-98ca-7b6841f35ee8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "14e6eb58-ec97-520f-a3b6-e469837fdc9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-73954" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=16 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $3$, the second equation by $2$, and adding the resulting equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{x}_{2}+8{x}_{2} & =48-2 \\\\ 23{x}_{2} & =46 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=2$  into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & =-1\\text{ } \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4(2) & =-1 \\\\ 3{x}_{1} & =-9 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=2$ into our third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} & =-18 \\\\ 4(-3)-3(2) & =-18 \\\\ -18 & =-18,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-3)+2=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02ee2ea2-2988-5741-bf62-6af834d17a2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387329} {:answer/id #uuid "9ce02f7c-04a9-5ac7-b531-6934a9fee5b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387330} {:answer/id #uuid "47167bc9-ef18-5b94-8896-7efb4e4107f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387331} {:answer/id #uuid "9e6b230b-33b0-5467-aa98-e7d3de1032f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387332} {:answer/id #uuid "70b95bea-e87e-572d-bb31-83417d9134f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02ee2ea2-2988-5741-bf62-6af834d17a2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387329} :answer-field/id #uuid "19b38c34-28a7-5285-b571-bb9d789beb82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "171d7adc-d40b-5e04-8b00-b146afdaeb83" :question/math-academy-id "q-73992" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-5 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=-10 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2.5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2.5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-5 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2.5\\,{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-2.5(-2)=8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=8-5=3.\n$$\n\nFinally,  substituting ${x}_{2}=3$ and ${x}_{3}=-2$  into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(3)+2(-2)=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=3$, and ${x}_{3}=-2,$ which means \n\n$$\n2{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}-2{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+3-2=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbc964ce-7179-5d39-90b8-63ab4b6a71b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321360} {:answer/id #uuid "b95f7d8c-a8d1-5fdc-8f38-7bb4d379a4e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321361} {:answer/id #uuid "5f2fd9b2-0430-5909-bccb-e8612211f708" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321362} {:answer/id #uuid "467e0bdc-9778-54b0-9938-f8de39e30cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321363} {:answer/id #uuid "fa89ef78-78f6-58cb-bf66-1f98d6d9f97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa89ef78-78f6-58cb-bf66-1f98d6d9f97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321364} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4413af7-ca5e-52fa-8023-3a23c164b23e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321359}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54baa5a4-47af-54e2-a17a-a1381c32da92" :question/math-academy-id "q-74032" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3}=-18 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -15 & -30\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{15}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this value into  the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-2(2)=-6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=-2$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1}+(-2)+3(2) & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1}+4 & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=1$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=2,$ which means \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}+2{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1+(-2)+2=1.\n$$"}]}
